  "changes": [
    {
      "start": 475,
      "end": 938,
      "before": "This guide answers three questions: what remains, which PR can proceed next, and what evidence makes it done. The [797-entry task register](remaining-work/units.json) supplies the exact tasks, source paths, dependencies, review budgets and acceptance conditions for every adopted unit. Each entry links to its detailed PR brief. Counts include implementation, generated work and verification; they are neither a feature percentage nor a guaranteed final PR count.",
      "after": "This guide answers three questions: what remains, which PR can proceed next, and what evidence makes it done. The [799-entry task register](remaining-work/units.json) supplies the exact tasks, source paths, dependencies, review budgets and acceptance conditions for every adopted unit. Each entry links to its detailed PR brief. Counts include implementation, generated work and verification; they are neither a feature percentage nor a guaranteed final PR count.",
      "reason": "[REMAINING-WORK.md:current-line-5] Align current task register to799 without changing completeness or count meaning. Preserve the complete surrounding historical guide; current-state wording is private proposed adoption only.",
      "plan_index": 0,
      "location": {
        "line": 5,
        "column": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "start": 940,
      "end": 1510,
      "before": "This execution snapshot is **SYSON-RUST-REMAINING/2026-10-31.20**, based on GitHub main `c9c55fb741f26adc46719b9e21f01aebf6d9be1b`. Completion contract **1.0.11** registers B25d1, B25d2 and M06a2 while preserving all 794 prior units, original dependencies and acceptance conditions, 55 historical records, holds and review budgets. [Team execution](TEAM-EXECUTION.md) remains unchanged; assignments grant no lease. The [immutable prior register](remaining-work/checkpoint-source-next-1.0.11/prior/register.json) and adjacent prior locks retain the complete .10 baseline.",
      "after": "This execution snapshot is **SYSON-RUST-REMAINING/2026-10-31.21**, based on qualified facade main `PENDING_QUALIFIED_F_MAIN`. Completion contract **1.0.12** registers M06a2a/M06a2b while preserving all 797 prior units, original dependencies and acceptance conditions, 55 historical records, holds and review budgets. [Team execution](TEAM-EXECUTION.md) remains unchanged; assignments grant no lease. The [adoption disposition](COMPLETION-CONTRACT.md#candidate-1012-adoption-disposition) requires actual generator and physical normative/snapshot readback. All 47 original cases and all 13 [loader controls](composition/identity_partition_prepare/test_loader_controls.py) must pass in normal and optimized modes; source presence grants no execution or feature acceptance. The [identity prior catalogue](remaining-work/checkpoint-identity-partition-1.0.12/prior/catalogue.json) binds the complete .11 baseline. The earlier [immutable source-next register](remaining-work/checkpoint-source-next-1.0.11/prior/register.json) and adjacent prior locks retain the complete .10 baseline.",
      "reason": "[REMAINING-WORK.md:current-line-7] Align current snapshot/contract/base to.21/.12, preserve immutable.10 source-next register and name actual.11 prior catalogue. Preserve the complete surrounding historical guide; current-state wording is private proposed adoption only.",
      "plan_index": 1,
      "location": {
        "line": 7,
        "column": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "start": 1512,
      "end": 2206,
      "before": "The register has 797 units. RR13a/RR13b are landed with the complete regular storage and fault suites plus real filesystem controls; their 31 cases pass in both modes. M06a2 must now restore the entire original identity/SnapshotStore integration and qualify real finite import, edit, save and fresh-process reopen. B25d1 retains the full corrected 200-line migration API and six original direct cases; B25d2 retains the complete 19-row corpus and all seven original cases. The [amendment](amendments/1.0.11-source-next.md) preserves the 400-production/900-authored-line caps. Neither registration nor local storage qualification accepts native, database, HTTP, UI or backend-restart durability.",
      "after": "The register has 799 units. RR13a/RR13b are landed with the complete regular storage and fault suites plus real filesystem controls; their 31 cases pass in both modes. M06a2 retains the full identity/SnapshotStore integration: M06a2a must complete real finite import, edit, save and fresh-process reopen, followed by M06a2b's mandatory release measurements. B25d1 [#237](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/237) and B25d2 [#238](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/238) are landed; the full corrected 200-line migration API, six original direct cases, complete 19-row corpus and all seven original corpus cases remain retained. The [identity amendment](amendments/1.0.12-identity-integration.md) preserves the 400-production/900-authored-line caps. The [constructor rules](composition/identity_partition_prepare/CONSTRUCT.md) retain complete proof lineage within `N <= 62` and 64 MiB of logical input/output accounting, without raising caps or claiming heap/RSS bounds. Neither registration nor local storage qualification accepts native, database, HTTP, UI or backend-restart durability.",
      "reason": "[REMAINING-WORK.md:current-line-9] Align799/newchild roles and actual landed B25d1/B25d2 status, preserving original API/case/corpus/native limits. Preserve the complete surrounding historical guide; current-state wording is private proposed adoption only.",
      "plan_index": 2,
      "location": {
        "line": 9,
        "column": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "start": 5804,
      "end": 6335,
      "before": "Work proceeds in parallel where prerequisites and source ownership permit. The next source scopes are [M06a2](prs/M06a2.md) and [B25d1](prs/B25d1.md), followed by [B25d2](prs/B25d2.md); each needs its own fresh lease and verification. The [batch36 queue](rereview-batch36-next-prs.md) remains historical. Use the [public contributor queue](../../CONTRIBUTOR-PR-QUEUE.md) and complete unit briefs for independent scopes; queue order does not establish readiness. Human issues #196\u2013#201 and every existing owner hold remain reserved.",
      "after": "Work proceeds in parallel where prerequisites and source ownership permit. The next identity source scope is [M06a2a](prs/M06a2a.md), followed by the separately required [M06a2b](prs/M06a2b.md); both remain children of [M06a2](prs/M06a2.md), and each needs its own admitted prerequisites, fresh lease and verification. B25d1/B25d2 are landed, with their parent acceptance obligations still open. The [batch36 queue](rereview-batch36-next-prs.md) remains historical. Use the [public contributor queue](../../CONTRIBUTOR-PR-QUEUE.md) and complete unit briefs for independent scopes; queue order does not establish readiness. Human issues #196\u2013#201 and every existing owner hold remain reserved.",
      "reason": "[REMAINING-WORK.md:current-line-25] Remove obsolete futureB25d1/B25d2 queue and dispatch exact new functional/measurement scopes only under fresh prerequisites/leases; retain all reservations. Preserve the complete surrounding historical guide; current-state wording is private proposed adoption only.",
      "plan_index": 3,
      "location": {
        "line": 25,
        "column": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "start": 22874,
      "end": 23199,
      "before": "| Model | 399 | Complete the assigned classifiers/features/operations, constructors, containment/inverses, references/proxies, visibility, derived state, caches/notifications, library lifecycle and custom schemas. Verify native results, ordering, foreign/stale handles, cycles and atomic late failure through real services. |",
      "after": "| Model | 401 | Complete the assigned classifiers/features/operations, constructors, containment/inverses, references/proxies, visibility, derived state, caches/notifications, library lifecycle and custom schemas. Verify native results, ordering, foreign/stale handles, cycles and atomic late failure through real services. |",
